# Brand, logo, and search on every page

## Goal

A person can tell which host they are on from the first paint. A crawler and an answer engine read the same name.

## Logo

1. Every HTML page shows the active host logo, linked to that host home.
2. CentroListo pages use `CentroListoLogoMark`. Institute pages use the logo from the brand layer (`app.logo.path` / `brand.logoPath`).
3. Account, login, and admin shells are included. A page with no logo is a bug.
4. CentroListo register and login use `PulsarSiteChromeEntry` (desktop and PWA). Do not replace that chrome with a bare form.

## Title

1. The document title contains the host name once.
2. A topic page uses `Topic | Host`. The home page may use one absolute title that already includes the host.
3. Do not emit `centrolisto | CentroListo` or `Host | Host`.
4. CentroListo titles go through `centrolistoDocumentTitle`. The entity string is `CentroListo`.

## Search and answer engines

Indexable public pages:

- A description, a canonical URL, and hreflang (`x-default` on the default locale).
- An Open Graph image with the host name.
- JSON-LD for the organization, with an absolute logo URL. The `name` matches the title host.
- A sitemap entry.
- On the CentroListo host, a line in `llms.txt` when the page answers a public question.

Private pages (account, login, register, admin, dashboard):

- `robots: { index: false, follow: false }`.
- The logo and a branded title still render.
- Do not list them in the sitemap or in `llms.txt`.

## CentroListo photos of people

1. Store still files under `public/centrolisto/wardrobe/`.
2. The garment carries the mark: a sage loop and a terracotta seed, small, stitched. No wordmark across the chest.
3. Reuse those files. Do not generate a new face per page, and do not call an image model during a request.
4. Alt text comes from `en.json`, `es.json`, and `pt.json`.

## Checklist

- [ ] The page shows the host logo on first paint, on desktop and on the PWA tree when one exists.
- [ ] The title names the host once.
- [ ] Indexable routes have description, canonical, hreflang, a share image, and JSON-LD.
- [ ] Private routes are noindex and absent from the sitemap.
- [ ] A new CentroListo photo of a person is a wardrobe file whose clothing carries the mark.
